@startuml
actor "User" as User
participant ":Pipeline / Project Library\n(Frontend)" as UI
participant ":PipelineStore\n(Zustand)" as Store
participant ":API Gateway\n(/classification)" as API
participant ":ProjectService" as PS
participant ":ClassificationService" as CS
participant ":JobQueueService" as JQS
participant ":Redis\n(broker + result backend)" as Redis

autonumber

== Preconditions ==
note over User, UI
  User is authenticated, a project is active, and a trained classifier
  is available (this session, or selected via the Project Library).
  Entry points: Pipeline page after Phase 1, or the Project Library
  "Apply Classifier" dialog. Steps 3-6 of the use case repeat this flow.
end note

== Dispatch ==

User -> UI : Define query (SearchQuery) + Run Labelling
UI -> Store : Read project_id + classifier_id
Store --> UI : project_id, classifier_id

UI -> API : POST /classification/label\n{ project_id, classifier_id, query }
API -> API : get_current_user (verify bearer token)
API -> PS : verify_project_owner(project_id, user_id)
API -> PS : get_classifier(project_id, classifier_id)
alt classifier missing
    PS --> API : raise ClassifierNotFound
    API --> UI : 404 Not Found
end
API -> CS : submit_labelling(project_id, classifier_id, query)
CS -> JQS : dispatch("...labelling_task",\n{ project_id, classifier_id, query })
JQS -> Redis : send_task (enqueue to broker)
JQS --> CS : job_id (AsyncResult.id)
CS --> API : job_id
API --> UI : { job_id }
UI -> Store : phase2JobId = job_id
UI --> User : Show progress (Labelling documents...)

note over UI, Redis
  SSE progress polling follows the same generic pattern shown for
  Topic Modelling (see "SSE Progress Stream"). Background task
  internals are detailed separately (see "Background Task Execution").
end note

== Completion ==

JQS -> Redis : get_status -> SUCCESS / FAILURE
JQS --> API : JobStatus { status, result }
API --> UI : SSE event (final)

alt SUCCESS, total_labelled > 0
    UI -> Store : setPhase2Result(result)
    UI --> User : Display labelling summary (topic + count)
else SUCCESS, total_labelled == 0 (Alt 6.1)
    UI -> Store : setPhase2Result(result)
    UI --> User : Summary shows 0 labelled — define a new query
else FAILURE
    UI --> User : Notify: custom query labelling failed. Please try again.
end

opt User defines another query for the same classifier
    note over UI : Repeats this Dispatch / Completion flow with a new SearchQuery.
end

== Exit to Visualiser ==

User -> UI : Click "Go to Visualiser"
UI -> Store : buildVisualiserPrefill(searchQuery, trainedClassifier)
UI --> User : Navigate to Visualiser with search parameters pre-filled
@enduml
